  "observations": [
    "PreparedOutboundConnection now has a distinct commit_staged_participant_with_held path for initial SIP on an empty checked/staged Core Session. It consumes the actual provisional route ticket, original current owned invocation, exact operation/revision/Participant/Connection/verified endpoint/address and endpoint-owner principal. It checks retained operation replay before signaling. The Session slot is reserved before activation, and the original supervisor owns the preparation through failure, cancellation, caller drop and final completion handshake. Ordinary native entrypoints still require their real peer; no replacement/source ticket or fake PeerAdmission is introduced.",
    "The initial invocation is an owned Box, consumed by Core. After signaling activation Core drops that initial invocation and its control lease before invoking the media callback. That callback can commit an observed answer and acquire fresh media/admission authority; it returns an owned Arc for the checked final policy. The reader-to-writer-to-fresh-reader fixture uses actual owned Tokio RW guards, including withdrawal, and proves neither initial nor final readers remain held after failure. The original policy deadline and principal expiry clip signaling; later guarded media admission retains its own engine deadline.",
    "OutboundParticipantPreparation is opaque Core-owned resource identity, not IO permission or media readiness. Its binding has the exact provisional incarnation and generation. The managed SIP exception in staged admission is available only through that exact owned object and a fresh explicit held policy. The registered controller must match its binding incarnation, original endpoint and owner. Bare callback success without a guarded controller cannot manufacture readiness. Wrong route/domain/withdrawal, dropped activation, setup failure with retained stale metadata and one-slot-before-second-activation fixtures pass.",
    "SipInitialParticipantContext binds the actual installed adapter and live SIP route to that initial preparation. It is separate from device replacement and uses weak owner/route links. Its one guarded controller uses the original CID/SID/Connection/generation and current host media policy; it neither manufactures a native Device nor claims replacement confirmation. Raw stream access and raw renegotiation refuse managed initial routes. Negotiated codec metadata remains distinct from remote consent, permission and actual decoded media flow.",
    "The positive fixture uses a real numeric-loopback UDP SIP peer and the actual SipAdapter. It receives the actual INVITE/SDP answer, waits for negotiated g.711-mu, installs actual guarded PCMU ports and admits one checked Participant/Connection. The final Connection principal is the endpoint owner. The activation receipt contains the exact SIP Call-ID observed on the wire. Ordinary Core hold refuses the provisional route before admission; raw streams/renegotiation refuse the admitted managed route. A retained logical operation cannot originate another call after admission. Session end produces one owned BYE dialog cleanup, and the captured context can no longer report negotiation afterward. This proves Core/adapter setup and custody, not canonical client dialing or decoded initial multiparty audio.",
    "The actual SIP fixture exposed a real provisional-lookup bug: the new path initially reused ordinary adapter_for, which correctly rejects NotInbound/unpublished routes. The final owned path now selects the adapter only through its exact provisional ticket at preparation and final readiness. Ordinary operational lookup is unchanged. Under the final registry/lifecycle/Session fences, the checked commit installs the Session binding and current endpoint principal before marking the Connection operational/visible and emitting its outbound hint. Early publication and a generic lookup bypass were not used as fixes.",
    "The final selected local regressions cover Service/server units, all3general signed/HTTP Session cases, public9, privateAI own-caller/context/return/restart and existing actual telephone PCMU movement/old-authority/route-loss. The older public-owned-shutdown refusal and private-duplex one-frame incident remain causally unestablished; these passes do not establish general provider availability."
  ],
